# Audiovisual Equipment Final Checklist

## Author
Joseph Okonkwo

## Context
This checklist serves as the final review of audiovisual equipment for the lecture hall in preparation for the dean of engineering's opening lecture during orientation day. Ensuring all equipment is functional and ready is critical to delivering a seamless experience for new students and staff members.

---

## Checklist Summary

### 1. **Projectors and Screens**
   - **Main Projector:**
     - [x] Verify the projector is properly mounted and secure.
     - [x] Test brightness and focus settings.
     - [x] Ensure HDMI and VGA input ports are functional.
     - [x] Confirm remote control functionality.
   - **Projector Screen:**
     - [x] Inspect for tears or damage (replacement screen delivered on 2026-04-02).
     - [x] Test motorized screen retraction.
     - [x] Ensure screen alignment with projector output.

### 2. **Audio Systems**
   - **Microphones:**
     - [x] Test wireless lapel microphones for sound clarity.
     - [x] Verify handheld microphones are charged and operational.
     - [x] Ensure backup microphones are available.
   - **Speakers:**
     - [x] Perform sound check on auditorium speakers.
     - [x] Verify balanced audio levels for all seating areas.
     - [x] Inspect wiring for wear or loose connections.
   - **Audio Mixer:**
     - [x] Test all input channels.
     - [x] Confirm volume and equalization controls are functional.
     - [x] Check compatibility with laptop and other external devices.

### 3. **Visual Systems**
   - **Monitors and Displays:**
     - [x] Verify all monitors are correctly positioned and powered on.
     - [x] Test connections to laptops and presentation devices.
     - [x] Ensure display resolution is set to 1920x1080.
   - **Presentation Software:**
     - [x] Run through slides using PowerPoint and ensure animations/functions work.
     - [x] Test compatibility with secondary monitors.
     - [x] Confirm updated graph requested by the dean on 2026-04-01 is properly displayed.

### 4. **Connectivity and Cables**
   - **HDMI Cables:**
     - [x] Inspect for damage or wear.
     - [x] Test connections to projector and laptop.
   - **Extension Cords:**
     - [x] Verify availability of at least 10 cords.
     - [x] Ensure cords are free of tangles and damage.
   - **Adapters:**
     - [x] Confirm availability of HDMI-to-VGA and USB-C adapters.
     - [x] Test functionality.

### 5. **Lighting**
   - **Overhead Lights:**
     - [x] Verify all bulbs are functional.
     - [x] Test adjustable brightness settings.
   - **Spotlights:**
     - [x] Ensure positioning illuminates the speaker’s podium.
     - [x] Test dimmer and on/off controls.

### 6. **Backup and Emergency Equipment**
   - **Spare Batteries:**
     - [x] Ensure availability for microphones and remote controls.
   - **Backup Projector:**
     - [x] Verify operational status (stored in logistics room).
   - **Power Backup:**
     - [x] Inspect uninterruptible power supply (UPS) unit.
     - [x] Test automatic switch functionality.

### 7. **IT Coordination**
   - **Wi-Fi:**
     - [x] Test connectivity for laptops and audience devices.
     - [x] Confirm access to campus network.
   - **QR Code:**
     - [x] Verify functionality of QR code linking to campus maps.
     - [x] Test readability using both iOS and Android devices.

### 8. **Final Walkthrough**
   - [x] Conduct a full walkthrough of equipment setup.
   - [x] Simulate presentation to ensure smooth transitions between slides and videos.
   - [x] Confirm all equipment meets performance expectations.

---

## Notes
- Replacement projector screen delivered and installed on 2026-04-02. Inspected and confirmed functional.
- Updated graph reflecting the latest research trends added to the dean’s presentation slides on 2026-04-01.
- All equipment tested in coordination with IT team to ensure seamless integration with campus network.

---

